# Pairs with SplitEventuallyLinked. Recovery never re-surfaces a marked split, so
# a root that loses its in-memory result before recording the intent never
# links the sibling.
# DEADLOCK: off is required: the stranded state has no successor, which TLC
# reports as a deadlock before it checks the liveness property.
MODULE: SplitEventuallyLinkedNoResurface
TARGET: SplitEventuallyLinked
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a marked split is never handed back to the root after a crash
PERTURBS: Resurface
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
    /\ marker /\ ~held /\ ~pending /\ ~linked
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: recovery never re-surfaces.
    /\ FALSE
    /\ marker /\ ~held /\ ~pending /\ ~linked
--- END
